
This repository contains the official supporting data and related resources for the systematic review paper "Node Importance Evaluation in Complex Networks Based on Graph Neural Networks: A Systematic Review" [1].

It primarily collects and organizes the topological statistical features of various real-world complex networks and Graph Neural Network (GNN) evaluation datasets discussed in the review. The goal is to provide a convenient and centralized data reference for researchers working on node importance evaluation, dynamic graph analysis, and heterogeneous graph modeling.

Some other databases [2-5].

[1] Kangzheng Huang, Ye Chang, Weibo Li, et al. Node Importance Evaluation in Complex Networks Based on Graph Neural Networks: A Systematic Review.
[2] https://public.websites.umich.edu/~mejn/netdata/
[3] https://snap.stanford.edu/data/
[4] http://konect.cc/networks/
[5] https://ogb.stanford.edu/docs/dataset_overview/
